1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,752
The Danish gambit trades pawns for open diagonals.

2
00:00:04,912 --> 00:00:09,365
White hits the center before Black can develop.

3
00:00:09,525 --> 00:00:13,977
The c pawn offers itself as a second piece of bait.

4
00:00:14,137 --> 00:00:18,590
Black takes, but the bishop on c four is already active.

5
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:23,203
The b pawn runs forward and looks like another free prize.

6
00:00:23,363 --> 00:00:27,815
White recaptures with the bishop and opens the b file.

7
00:00:27,975 --> 00:00:32,428
Black strikes the center to slow down the attack.

8
00:00:32,587 --> 00:00:37,040
White takes back and keeps every diagonal pointing forward.

9
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:41,652
The knight develops with tempo and protects the center.

10
00:00:41,812 --> 00:00:46,265
Black answers with a pin, but the lead in development remains.

11
00:00:46,425 --> 00:00:50,877
The lesson: activity is the compensation for sacrificed pawns.

12
00:00:51,037 --> 00:00:55,650
Would you play the Danish gambit?

